<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 226)</h2>
<p><b>Session recordings now replay the whole meeting</b> — sound and picture.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Notes → Replay Last Session Recording</b> plays the meeting back while the playhead follows what was on screen: every scrub, every clip change, re-performed in sync with the audio. You hear "the logo is too small" and you're looking at the exact frame they were.</li>
<li>Replay ends where the meeting ended — on the last thing discussed.</li>
<li>The <b>PDF note report</b> gains a SESSION MINUTES page: everything said, grouped by shot in the order discussed, timestamped to the frame.</li>
<li><b>Echo-cancelled recording.</b> Where the Mac allows it, what your speakers play — the call, the clip audio — is subtracted from what your mic records. A no-headphones room comes out as the room, not the room plus the call. If the system refuses, Asobi records plain mic audio; the meeting is always kept.</li>
<li>If the Speech permission dialog goes unanswered, the recording no longer waits behind it — audio and screen-log are kept, and if the transcript finishes late (you clicked Allow afterwards), the minutes merge in when they land.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
